### **1\. Labeling Your Samples** 

To maintain professionalism and ensure smooth uploads, your sample files must follow this exact naming format: SampleName\_BPM\_Key\_YourName\_\[CollaboratorName\].wav Example (solo): MidnightGlow\_140BPM\_Cmin\_ProdByK28.wav Example **(with collaborator)**: Stars\_98BPM\_Bminor\_ProdByJai\_**ProdbyK28**.wav (a) Use “ProdBy” before your name. (b) Use underscores to separate each element. (c) Do not use spaces or skip elements. Must include: \- Sample Name (clean and creative) \- BPM (tempo, e.g., 98, 140BPM) \- Key (e.g., Cmin, F#maj, Bminor) \- Your Name (with ProdBy) \- Collaborator(s), if any Mandatory Format - Files not labeled correctly will be rejected. 

### **2\. Tags** 

 Tags improve discoverability. Use tags related to: \- Genre: trap, drill, R&B, etc. \- Instrument: piano, flute, guitar, synth \- Mood/Vibe: dark, dreamy, ambient \- Influence: Travis Scott, Cubeatz, etc. Don’t over-tag. Keep it focused and specific. 

### **3\. Collaborators (feature coming soon)** 

If working with others: \- Add their names to the filename: Stars\_98BPM\_Bminor\_ProdByXYZ\_Prod.Mxrci.wav \- Ensure all collaborators approve the upload \- Manage revenue splits manually Beat22 does not do this 

### **4\. Outside Loops** 

Do NOT use: \- Splice, Cymatics, Looperman loops \- Loops from kits you don’t own \- Royalty-free packs you didn’t make Only upload 100% original content. Any violation may result in removal of the pack. 

### **5\. Copyrighted Material** 

Strictly prohibited: \- Movie clips \- YouTube samples \- Commercial music snippets \- Anything you don’t own Zero tolerance. Violators may face permanent account removal. 

### **6\. Payouts** 

\- Payouts via Bank Transfer (Indian accounts only) \- Need PayPal? Email: [support@beat22.com](mailto:support@beat22.com) \- Processed in 3–5 business days \- Manual handling may delay during high demand 

### **7\. Archive Policy** 

Kits may be archived if: \- Poor audio quality (clipping, noise, mixing) \- Copyrighted content \- Low-effort or inappropriate cover art \- Missing organization or wrong file structure Buyers who already downloaded archived kits will still have access. 

### **8\. Upload Help** 

Facing issues? Email: [support@beat22.com](mailto:support@beat22.com) We can manually upload or guide you Got feature ideas? We’d love to hear from you 

### **9\. Stems** 

Option 1: Separate Files (Preferred) \- Export all instruments individually \- All stems should start from bar 1 \- Name clearly: Piano.wav, Drums.wav Option 2: Combined Single File \- Play all parts one after another \- Attach a ReadMe.txt or visual guide \- File name: Loop1\_StemsCombined.wav Attach a short tutorial (inside Tutorials/ folder or via link) 

### **10\. Folder Structure Example** 

KitName/ │ ├── Artwork/ │   └── Cover.png ├── Main Loops/ │   ├── Loop1\_140BPM\_Cmin.wav │   └── Loop2\_142BPM\_Dmaj.wav ├── Stems/ │   ├── Loop1/ │   │   ├── Piano.wav │   │   └── 808.wav │   └── Loop2/ │       ├── Keys.wav │       └── Drums.wav ├── MIDI/ (optional) │   └── Loop1.mid ├── Tutorials/ (optional) │   └── StemsWalkthrough.mp4 └── ReadMe.txt (optional) Zip the full folder before uploading. 

### **11\. Licensing, Publishing & Splits** 

Licensing Fee \- Buyers get non-exclusive, royalty-free use, unless you specify otherwise \- No upfront fee charged by Beat22 \- You can also sell kits elsewhere (unless exclusive) Publishing Rights If your loop is used in a major/label release: \- You’re entitled to publishing/master splits \- You must handle negotiation directly with buyer Optional: Dynamic Splits If opted-in and used in a 1M+ stream track: \- Up to 25% publishing split (full use) \- 12.5% for partial usage Applies only when buyer is a Beat22 user. Reach out anytime via [support@beat22.com](mailto:support@beat22.com) 

**Thanks for being a part of [Beat22](http://beat22.com)** 

We’re building this platform for creators like you organized, original, and ready to impact the industry.
